completion_raw:
To terminate a C program, you can use the following methods:

1. Use the return statement: You can use the return statement to immediately exit the program. You can use this method in functions.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    return 0;
}
```

2. Use the exit() function: You can use the exit() function to terminate the program immediately. This function takes an integer status code as its argument.

```c
#include <stdlib.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello, World!\n");
    exit(0);
}
```

3. Use the return key: If your program is a command-line program, you can also terminate it by pressing the return key when you are done entering input. This will cause the program to exit automatically.

```c
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    char input;
    while (1) {
        printf("Enter a character (type 'q' to quit): ");

